WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.412
Step 6 collects the second
week and reads what changed.

2
00:00:03.412 --> 00:00:04.851
Seven notices now.

3
00:00:04.851 --> 00:00:11.113
A new post arrives with its own action
date from Microsoft, February 28, 2027.

4
00:00:11.113 --> 00:00:14.700
The SharePoint post is updated,
and its title says so.

5
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.787
The email incident from
week one is now closed.

6
00:00:17.787 --> 00:00:21.317
Step 7 builds the live
request without sending it:

7
00:00:21.317 --> 00:00:26.913
the first line is the exact URL a live run
would call, on the worldwide Graph host.

8
00:00:26.913 --> 00:00:29.694
Then it tries a next link on another host,

9
00:00:29.694 --> 00:00:33.790
and the kit refuses it, because
it isn't on the GCC Graph host.
